    "title": "Word Pattern II",
    "workload": "build 8 subjects of 30 chars once over a 4-letter alphabet (even indices have identical halves so the pattern CAN match, odd indices differ so the search fails only after exploring every split), then 500 punches of the full backtracking bijection search against pattern 'abcabc'; sink weights successes by iteration so both the success and exhaustive-failure paths are measured. NOTE: C hand-rolls an open-addressing string map and set with tombstones rather than the faster linear scan its <=3 live entries would allow, to keep the data structure like-for-like.",
